.toc div { margin-bottom: 3pt; }
</style></head><body>
<div class="title-page">
  <div class="t">GDL Fleet Management</div>
  <div class="s">User Manual</div>
  <div class="m">Version 1.0.0<br>22 September 2026</div>
  <div class="e">ERPNext 16.30.0 &middot; Frappe 16.29.0
    &middot; HRMS 16.15.0<br>gdl_fleet_extension 1.0.0</div>
</div>
<div class="toc"><h1 class="first">Table of Contents</h1><div>1. &nbsp;Introduction</div><div>2. &nbsp;System Overview</div><div>3. &nbsp;Fleet Roles and Permissions</div><div>4. &nbsp;Vehicle Master</div><div>5. &nbsp;Vehicle Types</div><div>6. &nbsp;Site and Location</div><div>7. &nbsp;Vehicle Booking</div><div>8. &nbsp;Vehicle Log</div><div>9. &nbsp;Odometer Management</div><div>10. &nbsp;Fuel Management</div><div>11. &nbsp;Maintenance</div><div>12. &nbsp;Preventive Maintenance</div><div>13. &nbsp;Corrective Maintenance and Asset Repair</div><div>14. &nbsp;Spare Parts Request</div><div>15. &nbsp;Spare Parts Issue</div><div>16. &nbsp;Tyre Management</div><div>17. &nbsp;Tyre Installation and Removal</div><div>18. &nbsp;Expense Claims</div><div>19. &nbsp;Mileage and Utilization</div><div>20. &nbsp;Accident and Incident</div><div>21. &nbsp;Reports</div><div>22. &nbsp;Dashboard</div><div>23. &nbsp;Notifications</div><div>24. &nbsp;Approval Workflows</div><div>25. &nbsp;Accounting and the Vehicle Dimension</div><div>26. &nbsp;Stock and Serial Number Handling</div><div>27. &nbsp;Common Validations</div><div>28. &nbsp;Troubleshooting</div><div>29. &nbsp;Frequently Asked Questions</div><div>30. &nbsp;User Role Matrix</div><div>31. &nbsp;End-to-End Fleet Process</div><div>32. &nbsp;UAT Checklist</div></div><h1>1. &nbsp;Introduction</h1><p>GDL Fleet Management runs on ERPNext 16. It is delivered as an extension app, gdl_fleet_extension, that builds on the fleet, asset, stock, HR and accounting functionality ERPNext already provides.</p><p>The guiding principle throughout was to extend the standard system rather than rebuild it. No ERPNext, HRMS or Frappe file was modified. Where ERPNext already had a capability it is used as-is; custom documents exist only where there was a genuine gap.</p><h3>1.1 &nbsp;What this means day to day</h3><ul><li>Your vehicles are standard ERPNext Vehicle records, not a separate master.</li><li>Trips are recorded on the standard Vehicle Log.</li><li>Maintenance uses the standard Asset Maintenance and Asset Repair documents.</li><li>Spare parts move through the standard Material Request and Stock Entry.</li><li>Expenses use the standard Expense Claim with its normal approval and posting.</li><li>Sites are standard ERPNext Location records.</li><li>All vehicle cost reporting reads the standard General Ledger.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Version</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Frappe Framework</td><td>16.29.0</td></tr><tr><td>ERPNext</td><td>16.30.0</td></tr><tr><td>HRMS</td><td>16.15.0</td></tr><tr><td>GDL Fleet Extension</td><td>1.0.0</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>2. &nbsp;System Overview</h1><p>The system is organised into one workspace, GDL Fleet, reachable from the app launcher. It gathers both the custom fleet documents and the standard ERPNext documents the fleet process depends on.</p><h3>2.1 &nbsp;Custom documents created for GDL</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Document</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle Booking Request</td><td>Submittable</td><td>Request, approve and assign a vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Fuel Entry</td><td>Submittable</td><td>Record a refuel and its odometer reading</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Tyre Installation</td><td>Submittable</td><td>Track a tyre from fitting to removal</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Accident Report</td><td>Submittable</td><td>Record an incident and its claim</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Mileage Deviation</td><td>Submittable</td><td>Raise and approve a mileage exception</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Vehicle Type</td><td>Master</td><td>Classify vehicles</td></tr><tr><td>GDL Fleet Settings</td><td>Single</td><td>All configurable thresholds and rules</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>2.2 &nbsp;Standard documents extended, not replaced</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Standard document</th><th>Fields added</th><th>What it is used for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Asset Maintenance</td><td>1</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Asset Maintenance Log</td><td>10</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Asset Maintenance Task</td><td>4</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Asset Repair</td><td>7</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Driver</td><td>2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expense Claim</td><td>5</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Expense Claim Detail</td><td>1</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Material Request</td><td>9</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Stock Entry</td><td>3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>20</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Log</td><td>13</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;The &#x27;Vehicle&#x27; field on accounting documents is not a custom field. It is created automatically by registering Vehicle as an ERPNext Accounting Dimension, which adds it to 57 accounting DocTypes at once.</div><h1>3. &nbsp;Fleet Roles and Permissions</h1><p>Eleven roles govern access. Assign them under Users, then the Roles tab. System Manager is deliberately not required for any fleet task.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Typical holder</th><th>What they can do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fleet Administrator</td><td>Fleet office</td><td>Full control of fleet master data and assignment</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Manager</td><td>Fleet head</td><td>Oversight, reports, accident management</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet User</td><td>General staff</td><td>Raise booking requests, view fleet data</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Driver</td><td>Drivers</td><td>Report incidents</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Validator</td><td>First approver</td><td>Validate booking and spare part requests</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Reviewer</td><td>Second approver</td><td>Review requests and incidents</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Approver</td><td>MTO / CEO</td><td>Management approval</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Finance User</td><td>FAS</td><td>Final financial approval, insurance stage</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Maintenance User</td><td>Workshop</td><td>Maintenance records and fuel entries</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Store User</td><td>Stores</td><td>Spare part approval and issue</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet HR Approver</td><td>HR</td><td>Mileage deviation approval</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Assignment of a vehicle and driver on a Booking Request is protected at permission level 1. Only Fleet Administrator and System Manager can write those fields, however many people can edit the rest of the request.</div><h1>4. &nbsp;Vehicle Master</h1><p>Purpose: the single record for each vehicle. This is the standard ERPNext Vehicle with GDL fields added.</p><p>Who: Fleet Administrator creates and edits. Fleet Manager and Fleet User can view.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet workspace, then Vehicle.</p><h3>4.1 &nbsp;Creating a vehicle</h3><ol><li>Open Vehicle and choose Add Vehicle.</li><li>Enter the Registration Number. This is also the document name.</li><li>Enter Make, Model, Fuel Type, Fuel UOM and Current Odometer.</li><li>Choose a Vehicle Type. This is mandatory.</li><li>Leave Vehicle ID blank to have it generated as GDL-VEH-00001.</li><li>Set Ownership Type, Site and the accounting dimensions.</li><li>Add registration, insurance and inspection dates.</li><li>Add scanned documents in the Vehicle Documents table.</li><li>Save.</li></ol><h3>4.2 &nbsp;GDL fields added to the Vehicle</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Options / Link</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Site</td><td>Link</td><td>Location</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Asset</td><td>Link</td><td>Asset</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Assigned Driver</td><td>Link</td><td>Driver</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Lessor / Rental Supplier</td><td>Link</td><td>Supplier</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Project</td><td>Link</td><td>Project</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Documents</td><td>Table</td><td>Fleet Vehicle Document</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Engine No</td><td>Data</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Department</td><td>Link</td><td>Department</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Cost Center</td><td>Link</td><td>Cost Center</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Type</td><td>Link</td><td>Fleet Vehicle Type</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle ID</td><td>Data</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Ownership Type</td><td>Select</td><td>GDL Owned / Leased / Rented / Other</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Status</td><td>Select</td><td>Available / Reserved / In Use / Under Maintenance / Unavailable / Sold / Disposed</td><td>Auto</td></tr><tr><td>Opening Odometer</td><td>Int</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Inspection Expiry</td><td>Date</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Manufacturing Year</td><td>Int</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Expected Monthly KM</td><td>Int</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Registration Expiry</td><td>Date</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Renewal Date</td><td>Date</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Registration Renewal Date</td><td>Date</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>4.3 &nbsp;Standard fields reused rather than duplicated</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field on screen</th><th>Standard field</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Registration Number</td><td>license_plate</td><td>Relabelled. Also the document name.</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Start Date</td><td>start_date</td><td>Relabelled</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Expiry</td><td>end_date</td><td>Relabelled, drives the expiry alert</td></tr><tr><td>Current Odometer (KM)</td><td>last_odometer</td><td>Relabelled, and now editable</td></tr><tr><td>Responsible Employee</td><td>employee</td><td>Relabelled</td></tr><tr><td>Chassis No, Colour, Make, Model</td><td>standard</td><td>Used as shipped</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Company, Policy No</td><td>standard</td><td>Used as shipped</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>4.4 &nbsp;Validations</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle ID X is already used by Vehicle Y</td><td>Duplicate Vehicle ID</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle ID cannot be changed once set</td><td>The ID is permanent by design</td></tr><tr><td>Manufacturing Year X is not valid</td><td>Outside 1950 to next year</td></tr><tr><td>Site X is a group Location</td><td>GDL or Farms chosen instead of a real site</td></tr><tr><td>Asset X is already linked to Vehicle Y</td><td>One Asset belongs to one Vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Opening Odometer cannot be greater than Current Odometer</td><td>Readings reversed</td></tr><tr><td>Row #N: Expiry Date cannot be before Issue Date</td><td>Bad dates in Documents</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Start date should be less than Insurance End date</td><td>Standard ERPNext rule</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Opening Odometer defaults to the reading entered when the vehicle is created. This is what the system falls back to if every Vehicle Log is later cancelled.</div><h1>5. &nbsp;Vehicle Types</h1><p>Purpose: classify vehicles so that bookings, mileage norms, maintenance rules, tyre positions and site requirements can be set per type.</p><p>Who: Fleet Administrator. How to open: GDL Fleet, then Fleet Vehicle Type.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Options</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle Type</td><td>Data</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Disabled</td><td>Check</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Requires Driver</td><td>Check</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Default Seating Capacity</td><td>Int</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Default Fuel Type</td><td>Select</td><td>No</td><td> / Petrol / Diesel / Natural Gas / Electric / Hybrid / CNG / LPG / Other</td></tr><tr><td>Description</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Configured on this system: Car</p><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Vehicle Type is mandatory on the Vehicle, so at least one type must exist before any vehicle can be saved. Tick Disabled to retire a type without deleting it.</div><h1>6. &nbsp;Site and Location</h1><p>Purpose: identify where a vehicle is based and where fleet activity happens. GDL sites are standard ERPNext Location records. No separate Site master exists.</p><p>Who: Fleet Administrator. How to open: GDL Fleet, then Sites.</p><h3>6.1 &nbsp;The approved hierarchy</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Location</th><th>Parent</th><th>Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GDL</td><td>-</td><td>Group</td></tr><tr><td>Head Office</td><td>GDL</td><td>Site</td></tr><tr><td>Farms</td><td>GDL</td><td>Group</td></tr><tr><td>Jamjee Farm</td><td>Farms</td><td>Site</td></tr><tr><td>Dochula Farm</td><td>Farms</td><td>Site</td></tr><tr><td>Dagapela Farm</td><td>Farms</td><td>Site</td></tr><tr><td>Gedu</td><td>Farms</td><td>Site</td></tr><tr><td>Samcholing</td><td>Farms</td><td>Site</td></tr><tr><td>Jigmeling</td><td>Farms</td><td>Site</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Vehicles and transactions attach to a site, never to a group. GDL and Farms exist for reporting roll-up only; the system refuses them. Because Location is a tree, a report filtered on Farms includes all six farms.</div><h3>6.2 &nbsp;Where a site can be recorded</h3><ul><li>Vehicle</li><li>Vehicle Booking Request</li><li>Vehicle Log</li><li>Fleet Fuel Entry</li><li>Material Request (spare parts)</li><li>Expense Claim</li><li>Fleet Accident Report</li><li>Fleet Mileage Deviation</li><li>Driver</li><li>Maintenance and tyres inherit the site from the vehicle</li></ul><h1>7. &nbsp;Vehicle Booking</h1><p>Purpose: request a vehicle, take it through approval, and assign a specific vehicle and driver.</p><p>Who: any Fleet User can raise a request. Only Fleet Administrator can assign the vehicle and driver.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet, then Vehicle Booking Request.</p><h3>7.1 &nbsp;Raising a request</h3><ol><li>Open Vehicle Booking Request and choose Add.</li><li>Confirm the Requester and choose the Employee travelling.</li><li>Set Site, and Project or Task if the trip belongs to one.</li><li>Write the Purpose and choose Usage and Priority.</li><li>Enter Required Date, Required From Time and Required To Time. For an overnight trip also set Return Date.</li><li>Enter Pickup Location, Destination and any additional stops.</li><li>Choose the Required Vehicle Type and the Passenger Count.</li><li>Save, then use the workflow action Submit for Validation.</li></ol><h3>7.2 &nbsp;Assigning a vehicle</h3><ol><li>Open the approved request.</li><li>Press Check Availability to list vehicles free for the whole period.</li><li>Set Assigned Vehicle and Assigned Driver.</li><li>Save, then use the action Assign Vehicle.</li></ol><h3>7.3 &nbsp;Fields</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Options / Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Requester</td><td>Link</td><td>Yes</td><td>User</td></tr><tr><td>Employee</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Employee</td></tr><tr><td>Department</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Department</td></tr><tr><td>Site</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Location</td></tr><tr><td>Project</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Project</td></tr><tr><td>Task</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Task</td></tr><tr><td>Cost Center</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Cost Center</td></tr><tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Small Text</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Usage</td><td>Select</td><td>Yes</td><td>Business / Official / Personal / Other</td></tr><tr><td>Priority</td><td>Select</td><td>Yes</td><td>Routine / Critical Business / Emergency</td></tr><tr><td>Passenger Count</td><td>Int</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Required Vehicle Type</td><td>Link</td><td>Yes</td><td>Fleet Vehicle Type</td></tr><tr><td>Required Date</td><td>Date</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Required From Time</td><td>Time</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Return Date</td><td>Date</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Required To Time</td><td>Time</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>From</td><td>Datetime</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>To</td><td>Datetime</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Duration (Hours)</td><td>Float</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Pickup Location</td><td>Data</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Destination</td><td>Data</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Additional Stops / Remarks</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Assigned Vehicle</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Assigned Driver</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Driver</td></tr><tr><td>Assigned By</td><td>Link</td><td>Auto</td><td>User</td></tr><tr><td>Assigned On</td><td>Datetime</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Assignment Remarks</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>Select</td><td>Auto</td><td>Draft / Pending Validation / Pending Review / Pending MTO/CEO / Pending FAS / Approved / Assigned / In Use / Completed / Rejected / Cancelled</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>7.4 &nbsp;Workflow</h3><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Document status</th><th>Who can edit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Draft</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet User</td></tr><tr><td>Pending Validation</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Validator</td></tr><tr><td>Pending Review</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td></tr><tr><td>Pending MTO/CEO</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Approver</td></tr><tr><td>Pending FAS</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Finance User</td></tr><tr><td>Approved</td><td>Submitted</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Assigned</td><td>Submitted</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>In Use</td><td>Submitted</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Completed</td><td>Submitted</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Rejected</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Cancelled</td><td>Cancelled</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr></tbody></table><table><thead><tr><th>From</th><th>Action</th><th>To</th><th>Role</th><th>Condition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Draft</td><td>Submit for Validation</td><td>Pending Validation</td><td>Fleet User</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending Validation</td><td>Validate</td><td>Pending Review</td><td>Fleet Validator</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending Validation</td><td>Reject</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Fleet Validator</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending Review</td><td>Review</td><td>Pending MTO/CEO</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending Review</td><td>Reject</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending MTO/CEO</td><td>Approve</td><td>Pending FAS</td><td>Fleet Approver</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending MTO/CEO</td><td>Reject</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Fleet Approver</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending FAS</td><td>Approve</td><td>Approved</td><td>Fleet Finance User</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Pending FAS</td><td>Reject</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Fleet Finance User</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Approved</td><td>Assign Vehicle</td><td>Assigned</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td><td>doc.vehicle and doc.driver</td></tr><tr><td>Assigned</td><td>Start Trip</td><td>In Use</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>In Use</td><td>Complete</td><td>Completed</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Approved</td><td>Cancel</td><td>Cancelled</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Assigned</td><td>Cancel</td><td>Cancelled</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td><td>-</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>7.5 &nbsp;Validations</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Required To Time must be after Required From Time</td><td>Times reversed</td></tr><tr><td>Required Date X is in the past</td><td>Only checked when the request is created</td></tr><tr><td>Return Date cannot be before the Required Date</td><td>Dates reversed</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle X cannot be assigned because its status is Y</td><td>The vehicle is under maintenance, unavailable or disposed</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle X is of type A but B was requested</td><td>Vehicle type mismatch</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle X is already booked by Y from ... to ...</td><td>Another approved booking overlaps the period</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Back-to-back bookings are allowed: a booking ending at 12:00 and another starting at 12:00 do not clash. Only genuine overlaps are refused. Draft requests do not hold a vehicle; only Approved, Assigned and In Use do.</div><h1>8. &nbsp;Vehicle Log</h1><p>Purpose: record a journey and the odometer reading at the end of it. This is the standard HRMS Vehicle Log with GDL fields added. No duplicate log exists.</p><p>Who: Fleet Administrator, Fleet Manager and the driver&#x27;s supervisor.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet, then Vehicle Log.</p><h3>8.1 &nbsp;Recording a trip</h3><ol><li>Open Vehicle Log and choose Add.</li><li>Choose the Vehicle. Starting Odometer fills in from the latest valid reading.</li><li>Choose the Employee and the Date.</li><li>Enter the Ending Odometer. Distance is calculated for you.</li><li>Choose the Usage and enter Start Location, Destination and Purpose.</li><li>Site, Department, Cost Center and Project default from the vehicle.</li><li>Save and Submit.</li></ol><h3>8.2 &nbsp;GDL fields added</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Options / Link</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Site</td><td>Link</td><td>Location</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Task</td><td>Link</td><td>Task</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Driver</td><td>Link</td><td>Driver</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Booking Request</td><td>Link</td><td>Vehicle Booking Request</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Project</td><td>Link</td><td>Project</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Small Text</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Department</td><td>Link</td><td>Department</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Usage</td><td>Select</td><td>Business / Official / Personal / Other</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Cost Center</td><td>Link</td><td>Cost Center</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Destination</td><td>Data</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Start Location</td><td>Data</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Starting Odometer</td><td>Int</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Distance Travelled (KM)</td><td>Int</td><td></td><td>Auto</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>8.3 &nbsp;Validations</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ending Odometer (X) cannot be less than Starting Odometer (Y)</td><td>Readings reversed</td></tr><tr><td>Current Odometer Value should be greater than Last Odometer Value</td><td>Standard ERPNext rule: the reading is below the vehicle&#x27;s current one</td></tr><tr><td>Starting Odometer cannot be negative</td><td>Negative value entered</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Distance Travelled = Ending Odometer minus Starting Odometer. The standard odometer field is reused as the ending reading, which is why the standard Vehicle Expenses report continues to work unchanged.</div><h1>9. &nbsp;Odometer Management</h1><p>The vehicle&#x27;s current odometer is maintained automatically. There is no separate odometer ledger to keep in step.</p><h3>9.1 &nbsp;Where readings come from</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Document</th><th>Field</th><th>When it counts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle Log</td><td>Ending Odometer</td><td>On submit</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Fuel Entry</td><td>Odometer</td><td>On submit</td></tr><tr><td>Asset Repair</td><td>Odometer</td><td>On submit</td></tr><tr><td>Asset Maintenance Log</td><td>Odometer</td><td>On submit</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Opening Odometer</td><td>Fallback floor</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>9.2 &nbsp;How the current reading is decided</h3><p>The vehicle&#x27;s Current Odometer is recalculated as the highest valid reading across all of those sources, never below the Opening Odometer.</p><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;This matters when a document is cancelled. Standard ERPNext subtracts the cancelled distance from the current reading, which is only correct if that document happened to be the most recent one; cancelling an older log would drag the odometer backwards. On this system the reading is recalculated from whatever is still live, so cancelling in any order gives the right answer.</div><h3>9.3 &nbsp;Correcting a wrong reading</h3><p>A Fleet Administrator edits Current Odometer on the Vehicle directly. ERPNext normally locks that field after creation; it was deliberately unlocked for this purpose.</p><h1>10. &nbsp;Fuel Management</h1><p>Purpose: record every refuel, keep the odometer current, and measure consumption honestly.</p><p>Who: Fleet Administrator, Fleet Maintenance User and Fleet Finance User.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet, then Fleet Fuel Entry.</p><h3>10.1 &nbsp;Recording a refuel</h3><ol><li>Open Fleet Fuel Entry and choose Add.</li><li>Choose the Vehicle. Fuel Type, UOM and dimensions fill in automatically.</li><li>Choose the Source: Supplier / Fuel Card, Bulk Tank, or Driver Paid.</li><li>Enter Quantity and Rate. Amount is calculated.</li><li>Enter the Odometer reading at the pump.</li><li>Tick Is Tank Full if the tank was filled to capacity.</li><li>Record the Supplier or the bulk tank Warehouse, and attach the Receipt.</li><li>Link the accounting voucher once it exists.</li><li>Save and Submit.</li></ol><h3>10.2 &nbsp;Fields</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Options / Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Link</td><td>Yes</td><td>Vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Driver</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Driver</td></tr><tr><td>Employee</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Employee</td></tr><tr><td>Date</td><td>Date</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Time</td><td>Time</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Source</td><td>Select</td><td>Yes</td><td>Supplier / Fuel Card / Bulk Tank / Driver Paid</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel Type</td><td>Select</td><td>Yes</td><td>Petrol / Diesel / Natural Gas / Electric / Hybrid / CNG / LPG / Other</td></tr><tr><td>Quantity</td><td>Float</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>UOM</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>UOM</td></tr><tr><td>Rate</td><td>Currency</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Amount</td><td>Currency</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Is Tank Full</td><td>Check</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Odometer</td><td>Int</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Previous Reading</td><td>Int</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Distance Since Last Fill</td><td>Int</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Supplier</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Supplier</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel Station</td><td>Data</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Source Warehouse</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Warehouse</td></tr><tr><td>Invoice / Receipt Reference</td><td>Data</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Site</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Location</td></tr><tr><td>Department</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Department</td></tr><tr><td>Cost Center</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Cost Center</td></tr><tr><td>Project</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Project</td></tr><tr><td>Company</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Company</td></tr><tr><td>Voucher Type</td><td>Select</td><td>No</td><td> / Purchase Invoice / Expense Claim / Stock Entry / Journal Entry</td></tr><tr><td>Voucher</td><td>Dynamic Link</td><td>No</td><td>accounting_voucher_type</td></tr><tr><td>Receipt</td><td>Attach</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Remarks</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>10.3 &nbsp;Accounting</h3><p>A Fuel Entry posts nothing to the ledger. It records the operational facts and points at the standard voucher that carries the money:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Accounting voucher</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Supplier / Fuel Card</td><td>Purchase Invoice</td></tr><tr><td>Driver Paid</td><td>Expense Claim</td></tr><tr><td>Bulk Tank</td><td>Stock Entry (Material Issue from the tank warehouse)</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>10.4 &nbsp;Fuel efficiency</h3><p>Efficiency is calculated only between two full-tank fills. Fuel consumed over an interval is everything added after the opening full tank, up to and including the closing one. The litres in the opening fill were burnt before the interval began and are excluded.</p><p>KM per unit = distance between the two full tanks / fuel added across the interval.</p><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;If a vehicle has fewer than two full-tank fills the report says so rather than showing a misleading number. Partial fills between two full tanks still count towards the litres. This is why Is Tank Full matters at the pump.</div><h3>10.5 &nbsp;Validations</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Quantity must be greater than zero</td><td>Zero or negative quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Rate must be greater than zero</td><td>Zero or negative rate</td></tr><tr><td>Odometer X is below the vehicle&#x27;s latest valid reading of Y</td><td>Reading moves backwards</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>11. &nbsp;Maintenance</h1><p>Vehicle maintenance runs on the standard ERPNext Assets module. The customer-facing Maintenance Schedule and Maintenance Visit documents are deliberately not used: they require a Customer and a Sales Person, which would mean inventing fake sales records for internal servicing.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>Standard document used</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Preventive plan</td><td>Asset Maintenance with Asset Maintenance Task rows</td></tr><tr><td>Preventive service record</td><td>Asset Maintenance Log</td></tr><tr><td>Corrective repair</td><td>Asset Repair</td></tr><tr><td>Parts consumed</td><td>Stock Entry, created by Asset Repair</td></tr><tr><td>Cost posting</td><td>Asset Repair posts its own GL entries</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Preventive planning requires the vehicle to be linked to an Asset, because ERPNext scopes Asset Maintenance to an asset. The Asset field on the Vehicle is optional, so vehicles can be created before Finance has produced the Asset records.</div><h1>12. &nbsp;Preventive Maintenance</h1><p>Purpose: service vehicles on schedule, by distance or by time, whichever falls due first.</p><p>Who: Fleet Maintenance User and Fleet Administrator.</p><h3>12.1 &nbsp;Service intervals are configuration</h3><p>Intervals live in GDL Fleet Settings and are read at runtime. Changing one is a desk edit, not a code change.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Service Item</th><th>Interval KM</th><th>Interval Months</th><th>Active</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine Oil</td><td>7500</td><td>6</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Engine Oil Filter</td><td>7500</td><td>6</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel Filter</td><td>10000</td><td>12</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Brake Fluid</td><td>40000</td><td>24</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Gear Oil</td><td>40000</td><td>24</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Tyre</td><td>20000</td><td>24</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>12.2 &nbsp;Creating a maintenance plan</h3><ol><li>Make sure the Vehicle has an Asset linked.</li><li>Make sure an Asset Maintenance Team exists with at least one real user.</li><li>Run the plan builder for the vehicle. It creates one Asset Maintenance record with a task per active rule.</li><li>Each task receives a standard periodicity from the month interval and a Next Due Odometer from the KM interval.</li></ol><h3>12.3 &nbsp;Recording a completed service</h3><ol><li>Open the Asset Maintenance Log for the task.</li><li>Set Service Date, Odometer, Service Provider, Labour Cost and Parts Cost.</li><li>Set Maintenance Status to Completed.</li><li>Submit. The task&#x27;s next due date and next due KM roll forward automatically.</li></ol><h3>12.4 &nbsp;How due is decided</h3><p>A task is due when either its Next Due Date or its Next Due Odometer is reached. The Maintenance Due report shows both, with days and kilometres remaining, and marks anything past its threshold as Overdue.</p><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Notice windows are configurable: currently 14 days and 500 km before due.</div><h1>13. &nbsp;Corrective Maintenance and Asset Repair</h1><p>Purpose: record a breakdown or repair, what it cost, what parts it consumed and how long the vehicle was off the road.</p><p>Who: Fleet Maintenance User and Fleet Administrator. Uses the standard Asset Repair.</p><h3>13.1 &nbsp;Recording a repair</h3><ol><li>Open Asset Repair and choose Add.</li><li>Choose the Asset. The Vehicle fills in automatically.</li><li>Set Maintenance Category, Service Type and Service Provider.</li><li>Enter the Failure Date, the Odometer and a Description.</li><li>Add consumed parts in Stock Items. ERPNext creates the Material Issue for you.</li><li>Enter Labour Cost and the repair cost.</li><li>Set Completion Date; ERPNext calculates Downtime.</li><li>Set Next Service Date and Next Service KM if the repair resets the schedule.</li><li>Submit.</li></ol><h3>13.2 &nbsp;GDL fields added to Asset Repair</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Options / Link</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Odometer</td><td>Int</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Labour Cost</td><td>Currency</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Service Type</td><td>Link</td><td>Vehicle Service Item</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Service Provider</td><td>Link</td><td>Supplier</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Next Service Date</td><td>Date</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance Category</td><td>Select</td><td>Corrective / Preventive / Accident</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Next Service KM</td><td>Int</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Asset Repair is already an accounting dimension document in ERPNext, so the Vehicle field on it is supplied automatically and its cost reaches the ledger tagged with the vehicle, with no extra work.</div><h1>14. &nbsp;Spare Parts Request</h1><p>Purpose: ask the store for parts for a specific vehicle or repair.</p><p>Who: Fleet Maintenance User raises; Fleet Validator, Fleet Reviewer and Fleet Store User approve.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet, then Material Request. No separate spare part document exists; this is the standard ERPNext Material Request.</p><h3>14.1 &nbsp;Raising a request</h3><ol><li>Open Material Request and choose Add.</li><li>Set Material Request Type to Material Issue.</li><li>Set Fleet Request Type to Spare Part, Tyre or Consumable.</li><li>Choose the Vehicle. Site, Department and Driver fill in automatically.</li><li>Link the Asset Repair or Maintenance Log if the parts belong to one.</li><li>Add the items, quantities and the warehouse.</li><li>Enter the Purpose and save.</li></ol><h3>14.2 &nbsp;GDL fields added to Material Request</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Options / Link</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Site</td><td>Link</td><td>Location</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Driver</td><td>Link</td><td>Driver</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Link</td><td>Vehicle</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Department</td><td>Link</td><td>Department</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Asset Repair</td><td>Link</td><td>Asset Repair</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Workflow State</td><td>Link</td><td>Workflow State</td><td>Auto</td></tr><tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Small Text</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Request Type</td><td>Select</td><td> / Spare Part / Tyre / Consumable / Vehicle Purchase</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance Log</td><td>Link</td><td>Asset Maintenance Log</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Vehicle is mandatory on a fleet request. This is controlled by Require Vehicle on Spare Part Issue in GDL Fleet Settings. Ordinary purchase and stock requests are completely unaffected: leave Fleet Request Type blank and nothing changes.</div><h1>15. &nbsp;Spare Parts Issue</h1><p>Purpose: physically issue the parts and have the cost land against the vehicle.</p><p>Who: Fleet Store User. Uses the standard Stock Entry.</p><h3>15.1 &nbsp;Issuing parts</h3><ol><li>Open Stock Entry and choose Add, or create it from the Material Request.</li><li>Set the type to Material Issue.</li><li>Set the Material Request reference. Vehicle, repair and project carry across.</li><li>Confirm the items, quantities, source warehouse and any serial or batch numbers.</li><li>Submit.</li></ol><h3>15.2 &nbsp;Traceability</h3><p>After issue you can follow the chain in either direction:</p><ul><li>Vehicle to the parts issued to it, through the Vehicle accounting dimension</li><li>Stock Entry back to the Material Request that authorised it</li><li>Stock Entry to the Asset Repair or Maintenance Log it belongs to</li><li>Item and Serial No to every vehicle it was ever fitted to</li></ul><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Stock quantity and valuation are handled entirely by the standard Stock Ledger. Nothing in the fleet app writes a quantity or a valuation. ERPNext&#x27;s own checks on availability, warehouse, item, serial and batch all still apply.</div><h1>16. &nbsp;Tyre Management</h1><p>Purpose: know which tyre is on which wheel, how far it ran, and whether it met its target life.</p><p>Who: Fleet Maintenance User and Fleet Store User.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet, then Fleet Tyre Installation.</p><h3>16.1 &nbsp;How tyres are identified</h3><p>A tyre is a standard ERPNext Item with serial numbers enabled. Each physical tyre is a standard Serial No. The Fleet Tyre Installation document records only what a Serial No cannot express: which position on which vehicle, between which two odometer readings.</p><h3>16.2 &nbsp;Positions are configurable</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Position</th><th>Spare</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Front Left</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Front Right</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Left</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Right</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Spare</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Positions can be restricted to a vehicle type, so a truck and a pickup can have different wheel layouts.</p><h3>16.3 &nbsp;Fields</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Options / Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tyre Serial No</td><td>Link</td><td>Yes</td><td>Serial No</td></tr><tr><td>Tyre Item</td><td>Link</td><td>Auto</td><td>Item</td></tr><tr><td>Brand</td><td>Link</td><td>Auto</td><td>Brand</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Link</td><td>Yes</td><td>Vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Position</td><td>Data</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>Select</td><td>Auto</td><td>Installed / Removed / Scrapped</td></tr><tr><td>Installation Date</td><td>Date</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Installation Odometer</td><td>Int</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Condition</td><td>Select</td><td>No</td><td>New / Retreaded / Used</td></tr><tr><td>Issue Stock Entry</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Stock Entry</td></tr><tr><td>Removal Date</td><td>Date</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Removal Odometer</td><td>Int</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Reason for Removal</td><td>Select</td><td>No</td><td> / Worn Out / Damaged / Puncture / Rotation / Accident / Manufacturing Defect / Other</td></tr><tr><td>Replacement Tyre</td><td>Link</td><td>Auto</td><td>Fleet Tyre Installation</td></tr><tr><td>KM Used</td><td>Int</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Target KM</td><td>Int</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Variance (KM)</td><td>Int</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Variance (%)</td><td>Float</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Performance</td><td>Select</td><td>Auto</td><td> / Within Tolerance / Below Tolerance / Above Tolerance</td></tr><tr><td>Cost</td><td>Currency</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Remarks</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><h1>17. &nbsp;Tyre Installation and Removal</h1><h3>17.1 &nbsp;Fitting a tyre</h3><ol><li>Issue the tyre from stock with a standard Stock Entry (Material Issue).</li><li>Open Fleet Tyre Installation and choose Add.</li><li>Choose the tyre Serial No and the Vehicle.</li><li>Choose the Position. The list comes from configuration.</li><li>Enter the Installation Date and Installation Odometer.</li><li>Record the Condition and link the issue Stock Entry.</li><li>Submit.</li></ol><h3>17.2 &nbsp;Removing a tyre</h3><ol><li>Open the submitted installation record.</li><li>Enter the Removal Date and Removal Odometer.</li><li>Choose the Reason for Removal.</li><li>Save. KM Used, Variance and Performance are calculated.</li></ol><h3>17.3 &nbsp;Tyre life</h3><p>KM Used = Removal Odometer minus Installation Odometer.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Target life</td><td>20000 km</td></tr><tr><td>Tolerance</td><td>±20.0%</td></tr><tr><td>Acceptable range</td><td>16000 to 24000 km</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Performance is flagged Below Tolerance, Within Tolerance or Above Tolerance.</p><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;The flag reflects distance only. The system never guesses why a tyre failed early: record that yourself in Reason for Removal.</div><h3>17.4 &nbsp;Validations</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tyre X is already installed on Y at position Z</td><td>One tyre cannot be on two vehicles</td></tr><tr><td>Position X on Y is already occupied by tyre Z</td><td>Record the removal first</td></tr><tr><td>Removal Odometer (X) cannot be less than Installation Odometer (Y)</td><td>Readings reversed</td></tr><tr><td>Position X is not configured for this vehicle</td><td>Position not in configuration</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Fitting a replacement in the same position automatically links it to the tyre it replaced, so the history of that wheel can be followed.</div><h1>18. &nbsp;Expense Claims</h1><p>Purpose: reimburse an employee for money spent on a vehicle, and get that cost onto the vehicle in the accounts.</p><p>Who: any employee raises; the standard expense approver approves.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet, then Expense Claim. This is the standard HRMS document.</p><h3>18.1 &nbsp;Claiming a vehicle expense</h3><ol><li>Open Expense Claim and choose Add.</li><li>Choose the Employee and the Company.</li><li>Choose the Vehicle. The fleet section appears and Site, Department, Cost Center, Project and Driver fill in from the vehicle.</li><li>Add expense lines, choosing the category in Expense Type.</li><li>Record the Supplier and Purpose, and attach the Receipt.</li><li>Save and follow the standard approval.</li></ol><h3>18.2 &nbsp;Expense categories</h3><p>Categories are standard Expense Claim Type records, not a fixed list in code. Adding one is a desk entry. The fleet categories created are:</p><ul><li>Fuel</li><li>Parking</li><li>Toll</li><li>Vehicle Repairs</li><li>Spare Parts</li><li>Vehicle Washing</li><li>Vehicle Registration</li><li>Vehicle Insurance</li><li>Other Vehicle Expenses</li></ul><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Each category needs a GL account mapped per company before a claim using it can be submitted. This is Finance&#x27;s decision and is done once, on the Expense Claim Type.</div><h3>18.3 &nbsp;GDL fields added</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Options / Link</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Site</td><td>Link</td><td>Location</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Driver</td><td>Link</td><td>Driver</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Small Text</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Receipt</td><td>Attach</td><td></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Supplier / Vendor</td><td>Link</td><td>Supplier</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Setting the Vehicle on the claim copies it to every expense line. That is what carries the cost into the ledger tagged with the vehicle.</div><h1>19. &nbsp;Mileage and Utilization</h1><p>Purpose: compare the distance a vehicle actually covered against what was expected, and raise an exception when the gap is too wide.</p><p>Who: Fleet Manager and Fleet Reviewer review; Fleet HR Approver approves exceptions.</p><h3>19.1 &nbsp;How actual distance is measured</h3><p>Actual distance is read from documents that already exist: the sum of Vehicle Log distances, or the spread between the lowest and highest odometer reading in the period across logs, fuel entries and maintenance records, whichever is greater. No separate odometer ledger is kept.</p><h3>19.2 &nbsp;How expected distance is set</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Precedence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Expected Monthly KM on the Vehicle</td><td>Highest - overrides everything</td></tr><tr><td>Mileage Norm for the vehicle type and site</td><td>Most specific norm wins</td></tr><tr><td>No norm configured</td><td>No baseline; deviation is not calculated</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>19.3 &nbsp;The calculation</h3><p>Deviation % = ((Actual KM − Expected KM) / Expected KM) × 100</p><p>Current threshold: ±10.0%. This is configurable in GDL Fleet Settings.</p><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;If no expected figure is configured the report shows a blank deviation rather than inventing a baseline, and the vehicle is never flagged.</div><h3>19.4 &nbsp;Exception handling</h3><ol><li>A Fleet Mileage Deviation is raised for each vehicle past the threshold.</li><li>The driver or user records an Explanation and submits it.</li><li>A Fleet Reviewer reviews it.</li><li>A Fleet HR Approver accepts or escalates it.</li></ol><table><thead><tr><th>From</th><th>Action</th><th>To</th><th>Role</th><th>Condition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Open</td><td>Submit Explanation</td><td>Explanation Submitted</td><td>Fleet User</td><td>doc.explanation</td></tr><tr><td>Explanation Submitted</td><td>Review</td><td>HR Review</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>HR Review</td><td>Accept</td><td>Accepted</td><td>Fleet HR Approver</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>HR Review</td><td>Escalate</td><td>Escalated</td><td>Fleet HR Approver</td><td>-</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>19.5 &nbsp;Tyre utilization</h3><p>Tyre utilization reads the Phase 9 fitment history and compares achieved distance against the configured target and tolerance. Nothing is hard-coded.</p><h1>20. &nbsp;Accident and Incident</h1><p>Purpose: record an incident, its investigation, the insurance claim and the cost.</p><p>Who: any Fleet Driver or Fleet User can report. Fleet Reviewer, Fleet Manager and Fleet Finance User handle the stages.</p><p>How to open: GDL Fleet, then Fleet Accident Report.</p><h3>20.1 &nbsp;Reporting an incident</h3><ol><li>Open Fleet Accident Report and choose Add.</li><li>Choose the Vehicle. Driver, Site and insurance policy fill in automatically.</li><li>Enter the Date, Time and where it happened.</li><li>Choose the Incident Type and describe what happened and the damage.</li><li>Tick Injuries Reported and record the details if anyone was hurt.</li><li>Record the Police Report Reference and attach the report.</li><li>Record the insurance company and Claim Reference.</li><li>Enter the Estimated Cost and expected Downtime.</li><li>Attach photographs.</li><li>Set Vehicle Status After Incident if the vehicle is off the road.</li><li>Save and use the action Report.</li></ol><h3>20.2 &nbsp;Fields</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Options / Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Link</td><td>Yes</td><td>Vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Driver</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Driver</td></tr><tr><td>Employee</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Employee</td></tr><tr><td>Date</td><td>Date</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Time</td><td>Time</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Site</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Location</td></tr><tr><td>Location Description</td><td>Data</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Incident Type</td><td>Select</td><td>Yes</td><td>Collision / Rollover / Fire / Theft / Vandalism / Third Party / Breakdown / Other</td></tr><tr><td>Odometer</td><td>Int</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Third Party Involved</td><td>Check</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Injuries Reported</td><td>Check</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Description</td><td>Small Text</td><td>Yes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Damage</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Injury / Safety Details</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Police Report Reference</td><td>Data</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Police Report</td><td>Attach</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Company</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Supplier</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Policy No</td><td>Data</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Claim Reference</td><td>Data</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Estimated Cost</td><td>Currency</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Actual Cost</td><td>Currency</td><td>Auto</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Downtime (Days)</td><td>Int</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Replacement Required</td><td>Check</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Asset Repair</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Asset Repair</td></tr><tr><td>Expense Claim</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Expense Claim</td></tr><tr><td>Cost Center</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Cost Center</td></tr><tr><td>Project</td><td>Link</td><td>No</td><td>Project</td></tr><tr><td>Photographs</td><td>Attach</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Supporting Document</td><td>Attach</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Remarks</td><td>Small Text</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Status After Incident</td><td>Select</td><td>No</td><td> / Roadworthy / Under Maintenance / Unavailable / Sold / Disposed</td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td>Select</td><td>Auto</td><td>Draft / Reported / Under Investigation / Insurance/Approval / Resolved / Closed / Cancelled</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>20.3 &nbsp;Workflow</h3><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Document status</th><th>Who can edit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Draft</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet User</td></tr><tr><td>Reported</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td></tr><tr><td>Under Investigation</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance/Approval</td><td>Draft</td><td>Fleet Finance User</td></tr><tr><td>Resolved</td><td>Submitted</td><td>Fleet Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Closed</td><td>Submitted</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Cancelled</td><td>Cancelled</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr></tbody></table><table><thead><tr><th>From</th><th>Action</th><th>To</th><th>Role</th><th>Condition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Draft</td><td>Report</td><td>Reported</td><td>Fleet User</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Reported</td><td>Investigate</td><td>Under Investigation</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Under Investigation</td><td>Send to Insurance</td><td>Insurance/Approval</td><td>Fleet Manager</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance/Approval</td><td>Resolve</td><td>Resolved</td><td>Fleet Finance User</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Resolved</td><td>Close</td><td>Closed</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td><td>-</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Actual Cost is not typed in. Link the Asset Repair that did the work and the cost is read from it, so the repair and the incident can never disagree. Submitting an incident with a status other than Roadworthy takes the vehicle off the road.</div><h1>21. &nbsp;Reports</h1><p>Eleven fleet reports were built. Four standard ERPNext reports are reused rather than rebuilt, because the Vehicle accounting dimension already makes them work per vehicle.</p><h3>21.1 &nbsp;Fleet reports</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Report</th><th>Answers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle Utilization</td><td>How hard is each vehicle working?</td></tr><tr><td>Mileage Deviation</td><td>Which vehicles are outside the expected distance?</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel Consumption and Efficiency</td><td>Litres, cost, km per litre, cost per km</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance Due</td><td>What is due or overdue, by date and by distance</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance Cost</td><td>What preventive and corrective work cost</td></tr><tr><td>Tyre Performance</td><td>Did each tyre meet its target life?</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Expense</td><td>Employee-claimed vehicle expenses by category</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Cost Analysis</td><td>Total cost per vehicle, split by source</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Cost Per KM</td><td>Cost per kilometre</td></tr><tr><td>Accident and Incident</td><td>Incident register with cost and downtime</td></tr><tr><td>Site Vehicle Requirement</td><td>Minimum required against what is there</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>21.2 &nbsp;Standard reports reused</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Report</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle Expenses (HR)</td><td>The standard HRMS fleet expense report, unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>General Ledger</td><td>Filter by Vehicle to see every posting</td></tr><tr><td>Budget Variance Report</td><td>Set Budget Against to Vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Profitability Analysis</td><td>Set Based On to Accounting Dimension, then Vehicle</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>21.3 &nbsp;Filters</h3><p>Every fleet report offers From Date, To Date, Vehicle, Site, Department, Driver, Project and Cost Center. Some add a checkbox such as Overdue Only or Flagged Only.</p><h3>21.4 &nbsp;What Vehicle Cost Analysis includes</h3><p>Every figure comes from the standard General Ledger using the Vehicle accounting dimension. Only debits to expense accounts on submitted, uncancelled vouchers are counted, so nothing is double counted.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Included</th><th>Excluded</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Expense Claims (fuel, parking, toll, washing, registration, insurance)</td><td>Depreciation, unless the entry is tagged with the vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Purchase Invoices (supplier fuel, workshop bills)</td><td>Anything not tagged with a vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Stock Entries (parts and tyres issued from store)</td><td>Draft and cancelled vouchers</td></tr><tr><td>Asset Repairs (corrective repair cost and consumed items)</td><td>Payments settling a payable</td></tr><tr><td>Journal Entries posted against a vehicle</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Cost per KM = total vehicle cost / distance covered in the period. A vehicle with no recorded distance shows a blank rather than a misleading figure.</div><h1>22. &nbsp;Dashboard</h1><p>The GDL Fleet workspace is the dashboard. Open it from the app launcher.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Card</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle Master</td><td>Vehicle, Driver, Fleet Vehicle Type</td></tr><tr><td>Operations</td><td>Booking Request, Vehicle Log, Fuel Entry, Mileage Deviation</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance</td><td>Asset Maintenance, Maintenance Log, Asset Repair, Asset</td></tr><tr><td>Spare Parts</td><td>Material Request, Stock Entry, Item, Warehouse</td></tr><tr><td>Tyres</td><td>Fleet Tyre Installation, Serial No</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses &amp; Incidents</td><td>Expense Claim, Expense Claim Type, Accident Report</td></tr><tr><td>Setup</td><td>GDL Fleet Settings, Vehicle Service Item, Sites, Cost Center, Department</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet Reports</td><td>All eleven fleet reports</td></tr><tr><td>Standard Accounting Reports</td><td>The four reused ERPNext reports</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Shortcuts: Vehicle, Booking Requests, Vehicle Log, Fuel Entries, Tyres, Incidents, Sites (tree view) and Fleet Settings.</p><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;The standard ERPNext fleet links remain where they always were, on the Frappe HR Expenses page under the Fleet Management card. Nothing was taken away.</div><h1>23. &nbsp;Notifications</h1><p>Thirteen alerts are configured as standard Frappe Notification records. The fleet app registers no background jobs of its own; Frappe&#x27;s own daily alert run drives the date-based ones.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Alert</th><th>Document</th><th>Trigger</th><th>Sent to</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Accident Pending Action</td><td>Fleet Accident Report</td><td>Value Change</td><td>Fleet Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Accident Reported</td><td>Fleet Accident Report</td><td>Submit</td><td>Fleet Approver, Fleet Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Booking Approval Pending</td><td>Vehicle Booking Request</td><td>Value Change</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td></tr><tr><td>Booking Assigned</td><td>Vehicle Booking Request</td><td>Value Change</td><td>requester</td></tr><tr><td>Booking Rejected</td><td>Vehicle Booking Request</td><td>Value Change</td><td>requester</td></tr><tr><td>Driving Licence Expiry</td><td>Driver</td><td>Days Before</td><td>Fleet Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Inspection Expiry</td><td>Vehicle</td><td>Days Before</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance Expiry</td><td>Vehicle</td><td>Days Before</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance Due</td><td>Asset Maintenance Log</td><td>Days Before</td><td>Fleet Maintenance User</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance Overdue</td><td>Asset Maintenance Log</td><td>Days After</td><td>Fleet Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Mileage Deviation Raised</td><td>Fleet Mileage Deviation</td><td>New</td><td>Fleet HR Approver</td></tr><tr><td>Registration Expiry</td><td>Vehicle</td><td>Days Before</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Spare Part Approval Pending</td><td>Material Request</td><td>Value Change</td><td>Fleet Store User</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Expiry alerts skip vehicles marked Sold / Disposed. The spare part alert fires only for fleet requests. Lead times come from GDL Fleet Settings, so they can be retuned without a deployment.</div><h1>24. &nbsp;Approval Workflows</h1><p>Four workflows are configured. Every transition names a role, never a person, so the approval chain can be changed from the desk.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Workflow</th><th>Document</th><th>Active</th><th>States</th><th>Transitions</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GDL Accident Handling</td><td>Fleet Accident Report</td><td>Yes</td><td>7</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>GDL Mileage Deviation Review</td><td>Fleet Mileage Deviation</td><td>Yes</td><td>6</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>GDL Spare Part Approval</td><td>Material Request</td><td>No</td><td>6</td><td>11</td></tr><tr><td>GDL Vehicle Booking Approval</td><td>Vehicle Booking Request</td><td>Yes</td><td>11</td><td>14</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>24.1 &nbsp;The GDL approval chain</h3><p>User → Validator → Reviewer → MTO/CEO → FAS → Approved, implemented on the Vehicle Booking Request as the roles Fleet User, Fleet Validator, Fleet Reviewer, Fleet Approver and Fleet Finance User.</p><h3>24.2 &nbsp;Spare Part Approval is supplied inactive</h3><p>A Frappe workflow governs an entire DocType; it cannot be limited to a subset of documents. Activating the spare part workflow would put every Material Request on the site, including purchasing and manufacturing requests, into the fleet state machine and replace their Submit button with workflow actions.</p><p>The workflow is therefore delivered switched off, with two safeguards already in place for when GDL decides to enable it:</p><ul><li>Every approval transition is conditional on Fleet Request Type being set, so ordinary requests never enter the fleet chain.</li><li>A bypass transition named Submit takes an ordinary request straight to Approved for Purchase Manager, Purchase User, Stock Manager and Stock User, so those roles keep a one-click path with the same button label.</li></ul><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Until it is activated, a spare part request is approved simply by submitting it.</div><h1>25. &nbsp;Accounting and the Vehicle Dimension</h1><p>Vehicle is registered as a standard ERPNext Accounting Dimension. This is what makes vehicle cost reporting possible without a separate cost ledger.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dimension document type</td><td>Vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Field name</td><td>vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Accounting DocTypes carrying it</td><td>57</td></tr><tr><td>Budget Against</td><td>Vehicle is available alongside Cost Center and Project</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Because ERPNext creates the field itself, the fleet app never declares a Vehicle field on an accounting document. Setting the vehicle on an Expense Claim, Purchase Invoice, Stock Entry, Journal Entry or Asset Repair carries it through to the General Ledger automatically.</p><h3>25.1 &nbsp;What this gives you</h3><ul><li>General Ledger filtered by vehicle</li><li>Trial Balance and financial statements by vehicle</li><li>Budget Variance Report with Budget Against set to Vehicle</li><li>Profitability Analysis based on the Vehicle dimension</li><li>Vehicle Cost Analysis and Cost Per KM in the fleet reports</li></ul><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;No document in the fleet app posts its own GL entry. Fuel entries, tyre records, incidents and bookings post nothing; value reaches the ledger only through standard ERPNext vouchers.</div><h1>26. &nbsp;Stock and Serial Number Handling</h1><p>All stock movement uses the standard ERPNext stock system. The fleet app writes no quantities and no valuations.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>Standard mechanism</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spare part request</td><td>Material Request, type Material Issue</td></tr><tr><td>Issue to a vehicle</td><td>Stock Entry, type Material Issue</td></tr><tr><td>Return to store</td><td>Stock Entry, type Material Receipt</td></tr><tr><td>Individual tyre identity</td><td>Serial No</td></tr><tr><td>Batch-tracked consumables</td><td>Batch</td></tr><tr><td>Stock balance</td><td>Bin and Stock Ledger Entry</td></tr><tr><td>Valuation</td><td>Standard ERPNext valuation</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><b>Note</b> &nbsp;Serial-tracked items require Activate Serial / Batch No for Item in Stock Settings. ERPNext 16 ships this switched off, and the fleet app deliberately does not change it, because it is a site-wide stock policy. Tyre tracking cannot be used until it is enabled. Note that once a serial transaction has been posted the setting can no longer be switched off.</div><h1>27. &nbsp;Common Validations</h1><p>A single reference of every rule the system enforces, and what to do about it.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Message</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Vehicle ID is already used</td><td>Use another ID or leave it blank</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Vehicle ID cannot be changed once set</td><td>The ID is permanent by design</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Site X is a group Location</td><td>Choose a specific site</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Manufacturing Year is not valid</td><td>Enter a year from 1950 onwards</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Opening Odometer cannot be greater than Current Odometer</td><td>Correct one</td></tr><tr><td>Booking</td><td>Required To Time must be after Required From Time</td><td>Correct the times</td></tr><tr><td>Booking</td><td>Vehicle is already booked from ... to ...</td><td>Pick another vehicle or slot</td></tr><tr><td>Booking</td><td>Vehicle is of type A but B was requested</td><td>Match the type</td></tr><tr><td>Booking</td><td>Vehicle cannot be assigned because its status is X</td><td>Choose another</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Log</td><td>Ending Odometer cannot be less than Starting Odometer</td><td>Correct it</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Log</td><td>Current Odometer Value should be greater than Last Odometer Value</td><td>The reading is below the vehicle&#x27;s current one</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel</td><td>Quantity must be greater than zero</td><td>Enter a real quantity</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel</td><td>Odometer is below the vehicle&#x27;s latest valid reading</td><td>Check the reading</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance</td><td>Vehicle has no linked Asset</td><td>Link the Asset first</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance</td><td>No active maintenance rules are configured</td><td>Configure rules</td></tr><tr><td>Spare Parts</td><td>Vehicle is required for a Spare Part request</td><td>Choose the vehicle</td></tr><tr><td>Tyre</td><td>Tyre is already installed on another vehicle</td><td>Record its removal first</td></tr><tr><td>Tyre</td><td>Position is already occupied</td><td>Remove the fitted tyre first</td></tr><tr><td>Tyre</td><td>Removal Odometer cannot be less than Installation Odometer</td><td>Correct it</td></tr><tr><td>Incident</td><td>The incident date cannot be in the future</td><td>Correct the date</td></tr><tr><td>Expense</td><td>Approval Status must be Approved or Rejected</td><td>Set the status first</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>28. &nbsp;Troubleshooting</h1><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cannot save a vehicle: Vehicle Type is mandatory</td><td>No Fleet Vehicle Type exists yet</td><td>Create the types first</td></tr><tr><td>The GDL Fleet tile is missing from the launcher</td><td>The browser cached the old workspace list</td><td>Hard refresh with Ctrl+Shift+R</td></tr><tr><td>Two tiles named Fleet</td><td>The legacy gdl_fleet_management app is still installed</td><td>Use GDL Fleet. The grey tile is the old prototype</td></tr><tr><td>A serial-tracked tyre cannot be transacted</td><td>Activate Serial / Batch No for Item is off in Stock Settings</td><td>Enable it through the Stock Settings screen, not the command line</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel efficiency shows no value</td><td>Fewer than two full-tank fills recorded</td><td>Tick Is Tank Full when the tank is filled</td></tr><tr><td>Mileage deviation is blank</td><td>No expected mileage configured</td><td>Set Expected Monthly KM on the vehicle or add a Mileage Norm</td></tr><tr><td>Cost per KM is blank</td><td>No distance recorded in the period</td><td>Record Vehicle Logs or fuel entries with odometer readings</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicle Cost Analysis shows zero</td><td>Vouchers were posted without the vehicle tag</td><td>Set the Vehicle on the document before submitting</td></tr><tr><td>An expense claim will not submit</td><td>The expense category has no account mapped for the company</td><td>Map the account on the Expense Claim Type</td></tr><tr><td>Cannot create a maintenance plan</td><td>The vehicle has no Asset, or the maintenance team has no valid user</td><td>Link an Asset and check the team members exist as users</td></tr><tr><td>Tests fail with a Redis connection error</td><td>The bench Redis instances are not running</td><td>Run bench start in another terminal</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>29. &nbsp;Frequently Asked Questions</h1><table><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Why is the vehicle named after its registration number?</td><td>That is standard ERPNext behaviour and it was kept. The GDL Vehicle ID is a separate, permanent internal identifier.</td></tr><tr><td>Can I change a Vehicle ID?</td><td>No. It is permanent once set, so that historical records always mean the same vehicle.</td></tr><tr><td>Why can I edit the Current Odometer now?</td><td>ERPNext locks it after creation. It was deliberately unlocked so that a Fleet Administrator can correct a wrong reading.</td></tr><tr><td>What happens if I cancel an old Vehicle Log?</td><td>Nothing bad. The vehicle&#x27;s odometer is recalculated from whatever is still live, so an old cancellation does not drag it backwards.</td></tr><tr><td>Why does fuel efficiency need full tanks?</td><td>Between two partial fills the amount left in the tank is unknown, so any figure would be a guess. Full-to-full is the only honest measure.</td></tr><tr><td>Do I need an Asset for every vehicle?</td><td>Only for preventive maintenance planning, which ERPNext scopes to an asset. Vehicles can be created and used without one.</td></tr><tr><td>Why is the spare part workflow switched off?</td><td>Activating it would govern every Material Request on the site, not just fleet ones. The safeguards are in place; it is GDL&#x27;s decision to switch on.</td></tr><tr><td>Where did the old Fleet Management tile go?</td><td>It is still there. It belongs to the legacy prototype app and should not be used.</td></tr><tr><td>Can I change the service intervals?</td><td>Yes, in GDL Fleet Settings. They are configuration, not code.</td></tr><tr><td>Can I change the tyre target or the mileage threshold?</td><td>Yes, both are in GDL Fleet Settings.</td></tr><tr><td>Does the fleet app post its own accounting entries?</td><td>No. Every posting is made by a standard ERPNext voucher.</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>30. &nbsp;User Role Matrix</h1><table><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Roles that can do it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Create and edit vehicles</td><td>Fleet Administrator, System Manager</td></tr><tr><td>View vehicles and reports</td><td>All fleet roles</td></tr><tr><td>Raise a booking request</td><td>Fleet User, Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Validate a booking</td><td>Fleet Validator</td></tr><tr><td>Review a booking</td><td>Fleet Reviewer</td></tr><tr><td>Management approval</td><td>Fleet Approver</td></tr><tr><td>Financial approval</td><td>Fleet Finance User</td></tr><tr><td>Assign a vehicle and driver</td><td>Fleet Administrator only (permission level 1)</td></tr><tr><td>Record a Vehicle Log</td><td>Fleet Manager, Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Record a fuel entry</td><td>Fleet Administrator, Fleet Maintenance User, Fleet Finance User</td></tr><tr><td>Record maintenance</td><td>Fleet Maintenance User, Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Approve a spare part request</td><td>Fleet Validator, Fleet Reviewer, Fleet Store User</td></tr><tr><td>Issue spare parts</td><td>Fleet Store User, Stock User, Stock Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Record a tyre fitting</td><td>Fleet Maintenance User, Fleet Store User, Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Report an incident</td><td>Fleet Driver, Fleet User, and above</td></tr><tr><td>Investigate an incident</td><td>Fleet Reviewer, Fleet Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance stage</td><td>Fleet Finance User</td></tr><tr><td>Close an incident</td><td>Fleet Administrator</td></tr><tr><td>Approve a mileage deviation</td><td>Fleet HR Approver</td></tr><tr><td>Change fleet configuration</td><td>Fleet Administrator, System Manager</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>31. &nbsp;End-to-End Fleet Process</h1><p>A worked example following one journey from request to cost.</p><h3>31.1 &nbsp;1. Setup, done once</h3><ol><li>Create the Fleet Vehicle Types.</li><li>Check the site tree under Sites.</li><li>Create vehicles and drivers.</li><li>Map GL accounts to the fleet expense categories.</li><li>Review the intervals and thresholds in GDL Fleet Settings.</li><li>Assign roles to users.</li></ol><h3>31.2 &nbsp;2. A trip</h3><ol><li>A farm supervisor raises a Vehicle Booking Request for a 4WD Pickup to Jamjee Farm next Tuesday.</li><li>It passes Validator, Reviewer, MTO/CEO and FAS.</li><li>The Fleet Administrator presses Check Availability, assigns a free vehicle and a driver, and uses Assign Vehicle.</li><li>On the day the booking moves to In Use, and afterwards to Completed.</li><li>The driver&#x27;s Vehicle Log records 20,150 to 20,610 km, purpose and destination. The vehicle&#x27;s odometer updates to 20,610 on submit.</li></ol><h3>31.3 &nbsp;3. Fuel</h3><ol><li>The driver fills up on the way back and a Fleet Fuel Entry records 45 litres at 20,610 km with Is Tank Full ticked.</li><li>The fuel card invoice arrives and is entered as a Purchase Invoice with the vehicle set.</li><li>The Fuel Entry is linked to that invoice.</li><li>Once a second full tank is recorded, the Fuel Consumption report shows km per litre for the interval.</li></ol><h3>31.4 &nbsp;4. Maintenance</h3><ol><li>At 27,650 km the Engine Oil task falls due; the Maintenance Due report shows it.</li><li>The workshop books the service and records an Asset Maintenance Log with the odometer, labour and parts cost.</li><li>On submit the next due date and next due KM roll forward by the configured interval.</li></ol><h3>31.5 &nbsp;5. Parts</h3><ol><li>The workshop raises a Material Request of type Material Issue with Fleet Request Type Spare Part and the vehicle set.</li><li>Stores issues the parts with a Stock Entry, which carries the vehicle across.</li><li>The cost lands in the ledger tagged with the vehicle.</li></ol><h3>31.6 &nbsp;6. Cost</h3><ol><li>At month end, Vehicle Cost Analysis shows the vehicle&#x27;s total cost split by expense claims, purchase invoices, stock issues and repairs.</li><li>Vehicle Cost Per KM divides that by the distance covered.</li><li>Mileage Deviation shows whether the vehicle ran within its expected range.</li></ol><h1>32. &nbsp;UAT Checklist</h1><p>Tick each item on the live system. Every one of these is also covered by an automated test.</p><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Check</th><th>Expected result</th><th>Pass</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Open the GDL Fleet workspace</td><td>Nine cards appear</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Check the site tree</td><td>GDL, Head Office, Farms and six farms</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Create a Fleet Vehicle Type</td><td>Saves</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Create a vehicle with no Vehicle Type</td><td>Mandatory field error</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Create a vehicle, leaving Vehicle ID blank</td><td>ID auto-fills as GDL-VEH-000xx</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Edit the Vehicle ID afterwards</td><td>Refused as immutable</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Set Site to Farms</td><td>Refused as a group Location</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Add vehicle documents with various expiry dates</td><td>Status shows Expired, Expiring Soon, Valid, Not Applicable</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Raise a booking with the end time before the start</td><td>Refused</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Raise two overlapping bookings for one vehicle</td><td>Second is refused</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Raise back-to-back bookings</td><td>Both accepted</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Press Check Availability</td><td>Only free vehicles listed</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Walk a booking through the full approval chain</td><td>Reaches Approved</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>Assign a vehicle and driver</td><td>Status becomes Assigned</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>Submit a Vehicle Log</td><td>Vehicle odometer updates</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>Cancel an older Vehicle Log</td><td>Vehicle odometer does NOT change</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Cancel the newest Vehicle Log</td><td>Odometer falls back to the previous reading</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>Record a fuel entry below the current odometer</td><td>Refused</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Record two full-tank fills</td><td>Fuel efficiency appears</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>Record only partial fills</td><td>Efficiency withheld with an explanation</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>Create a maintenance plan for a vehicle with an Asset</td><td>Asset Maintenance created with one task per rule</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>Drive past a KM threshold</td><td>Maintenance Due shows it as Overdue</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>23</td><td>Submit an Asset Maintenance Log</td><td>Next due date and KM roll forward</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>24</td><td>Change an interval in GDL Fleet Settings</td><td>Next due KM changes accordingly</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>Raise a fleet Material Request without a vehicle</td><td>Refused</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>Raise an ordinary Material Request</td><td>Unaffected, saves normally</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>27</td><td>Issue more stock than is available</td><td>Standard ERPNext refuses it</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>Fit a tyre to an occupied position</td><td>Refused</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>29</td><td>Fit one tyre to two vehicles</td><td>Refused</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>Remove a tyre at 15,000 km</td><td>Flagged Below Tolerance</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>Change the tyre target to 40,000 km</td><td>The same tyre re-flags</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>Submit an expense claim with a vehicle</td><td>GL entries carry the vehicle dimension</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>Run General Ledger filtered by vehicle</td><td>Shows the tagged entries</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>Run all eleven fleet reports</td><td>All return columns without error</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>Report an incident with status Under Maintenance</td><td>The vehicle is taken off the road</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>Walk an incident through its workflow</td><td>Reaches Closed</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>Raise a mileage deviation past the threshold</td><td>A Fleet Mileage Deviation is created</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>Log in as a Fleet User</td><td>Cannot assign a vehicle to a booking</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>Check the notification list</td><td>Thirteen GDL Fleet alerts, all enabled</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>Confirm the HR Expenses page</td><td>The standard Fleet Management card is intact</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><h1>Revision History</h1><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Date</th><th>Change</th><th>Author</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1.0</td><td>22 September 2026</td><td>First release. Covers the delivered implementation of phases 1 to 16.</td><td>GDL Fleet Implementation</td></tr></tbody></table></body></html>